WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.990
From buzzworthy biopics to high-profile action
thrillers, Netflix is roaring into 2023.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:11.880
Here are 25 of the most-anticipated films
coming our way on Netflix this year.

00:00:12.282 --> 00:00:18.020
After finding critical success with 2020's
Extraction, director Sam Hargrave is back,

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.109
along with the Russo Brothers, with Extraction
2.

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:26.900
Due to hit Netflix sometime in 2023, Extraction
2 will again focus on Chris Hemsworth's Tyler

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.490
Rake, a black ops mercenary tasked with a
life-or-death mission.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:35.960
"With the title of "2" behind your name, you
have to bring at least twice the action."

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:41.100
Extraction was a refreshing entry in the action
genre, and Hemsworth delivered a career-defining

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.890
performance, for which he received praise
from audiences and critics alike.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.140
The film became one of Netflix's most-watched
originals ever, reaching 99 million households

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.450
in its first month on the streaming service.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:01:01.870
"You drown not by falling into the river,
but by staying submerged in it."

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.650
Besides Hemsworth, a definitive cast list
hasn't been made public, though Golshifteh

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:11.050
Farahani is set to reprise her role of Nik
Khan, Tyler's partner.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.700
No release date has been pinned down, but
filming is said to have wrapped last April.

00:01:15.453 --> 00:01:20.900
It's been 23 years since Peter Lord and Nick
Park created Chicken Run, a triumphant piece

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.381
of stop-motion animation.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:28.430
Chicken Run remains the highest-grossing stop-motion
film ever, raking in over $227 million at

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.530
the box office.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:34.110
Chicken Run: Dawn of the Nugget was greenlit
in 2018 by StudioCanal, and Netflix acquired

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.110
the rights in 2020.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.570
The film will focus on Ginger and her friends
after they escape Tweedy's farm.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.380
"Is it as good as you imagined?"

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.380
"No."

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.380
"No?"

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.380
"It's better."

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.469
Jane Horrocks, Imelda Staunton, and Lynn Ferguson
are the only original actors to reprise their

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:50.070
roles from the first movie.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:54.150
But given the critical response to the first
film, we should expect another brilliant,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.060
entertaining story from Lord and Park.

00:01:56.332 --> 00:02:01.801
Adaptations of books by renowned children's
author Roald Dahl have often become movie classics.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:06.719
Beginning with 1971's Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate
Factory all the way to Roald Dahl's The Witches

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:11.000
" in 2020, Dahl's work has been a linchpin
in cinema for five decades.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.500
In 2021, Netflix acquired the rights to the
Roald Dahl Story Company, paying over $680

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.620
million dollars for the author's bibliography.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:24.340
First up is The Wonderful Story of Henry Sugar,
helmed by acclaimed director Wes Anderson.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.860
Published in 1977, The Wonderful Story of
Henry Sugar follows Sugar, a gambler who dares

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.440
to use meditation to count cards.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:37.462
Anderson's adaptation will explore the destruction
of greed that Dahl's adult-skewed fairy tale examined.

00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:42.470
With Benedict Cumberbatch set to play Sugar,
and a supporting cast of Ralph Fiennes, Dev

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:47.670
Patel, and Ben Kingsley, The Wonderful Story
of Henry Sugar should be a marvelous entry

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.579
in the Dahl cinematic universe.

00:02:50.141 --> 00:02:54.890
Though it hit theaters for a limited release
on December 23, Scott Cooper's The Pale Blue

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:59.560
Eye was the first original movie to stream
on Netflix in 2023.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.270
Netflix seems to be starting the year off
with a lot of corpses and conspiracies.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:07.860
The Pale Blue Eye doesn't skimp on brutality,
which adds another layer of darkness to Cooper's

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:08.860
period piece.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.080
"It is a whodunnit."

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:16.370
"It's a fictional story about a series of
murders that take place at West Point."

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:21.910
Set in 1830, The Pale Blue Eye follows Augustus
Landor, played by Christian Bale, as he investigates

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.680
murders within the U.S. military, alongside
a young Edgar Allan Poe, played by Harry Melling.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:33.840
"With enough patience, a suspect will often
interrogate himself."

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.349
The movie is based on Louis Bayard's 2003
novel of the same name and has a terrific

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:43.418
cast that includes Gillian Anderson and Robert
Duvall among many other standouts.

00:03:43.911 --> 00:03:48.599
Fans of the Beverly Hills Cop franchise have
been waiting 28 years for another installment

00:03:48.599 --> 00:03:52.140
and, in 2023, their time will finally come.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:57.269
Beverly Hills Cop: Axel Foley marks another
turn in Murphy's ongoing career renaissance.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:01.280
Hoping to capitalize on the acclaim he received
for his performances in Dolemite Is My Name

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.430
and Coming 2 America, audiences can only hope
that the comedian can slip back into the persona

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.140
of his most beloved character.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.400
"Yes, you have a reservation for an Axel Foley."

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.610
The story follows Axel as he comes back to
Beverly Hills to sniff out corruption in his

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.610
old police department.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.950
"Can you put this in a good spot?

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.269
All this s— happened the last time I parked
here."

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:25.431
Many of the franchise's original cast, including
Judge Reinhold and Bronson Pinchot, are set

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:30.060
to return, while Taylour Paige, Kevin Bacon,
and Joseph Gordon-Levitt will take on brand

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.090
new characters.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.639
Beverly Hills Cop has a storied legacy, with
the original film consistently labeled as

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:41.661
one of the funniest movies ever made, so Beverly
Hills Cop: Axel Foley has a lot to live up to.

00:04:41.661 --> 00:04:46.940
It'll be exciting to see the old gang back
in action for the first time in almost 30 years.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:51.190
Not much is known about the film adaptation
of Matt Kindt's comic book series Dept.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.440
H, though it's set to hit Netflix sometime
this year.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:58.710
Alice Waddington is slated to direct the film,
her first credit since her feature debut,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.560
Paradise Hills, in 2019.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:05.500
Dept. H revolves around Mia, a special investigator
hired to derail a saboteur's plan at a deep

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.009
sea research facility.

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:11.900
The series traverses a long, complicated crime
scene that plays out like a nautical game

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:17.442
of Clue, where suspects must prove their innocence
while surviving against the creatures surrounding them.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:22.050
How Waddington will condense Kindt's work
into one feature film will be something worth

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.190
keeping note of.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.800
No cast list has yet been released.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.060
Kindt's series ran for almost two full years.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.030
Given that the comic doesn't have the biggest
fanbase, that leaves the door wide open for

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.700
Waddington to make the source material her
own.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:41.308
It's one of the most-anticipated Netflix releases
and comic book adaptations of 2023.

00:05:41.551 --> 00:05:47.160
In one of Netflix's most high-profile releases
of 2023, Tom Harper's Heart of Stone has garnered

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:52.960
a lot of attention thanks to its illustrious
cast, which includes Gal Gadot and Jamie Dornan

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:53.960
in the leading roles.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.490
Heart of Stone will be Harper's first directorial
effort since The Aeronauts in 2019.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:03.330
The story revolves around Rachel Stone, a
CIA agent navigating altercations with dangerous

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.600
global powers.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.580
"Rachel Stone lives off the adrenaline.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.740
She's addicted to it."

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.870
Most of the plot is being kept under wraps.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.500
We just know that it's a spy action thriller.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:20.693
Sophie Okonedo, Matthias Schweighöfer, Jing
Lusi, and Alia Bhatt are set to play supporting roles.

00:06:20.693 --> 00:06:27.310
Written, directed, and starring Jerry Seinfeld,
Unfrosted: The Pop-Tart Story is one of Netflix's

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:30.060
most anticipated comedies of the upcoming
year.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.669
Seinfeld has directed before, including episodes
of his own show, Comedians in Cars Getting

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:36.960
Coffee, and two of Colin Quinn's stand-up
specials.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.699
Netflix won the rights to the film in 2021,
the premise of which stems from Seinfeld's

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:43.530
own joke about the Pop-Tart's inception.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:46.630
"They can't go stale, 'cause they were never
fresh."

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:52.230
In the story, two breakfast cereal titans,
Kellogg's and Post, duke it out, competing

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:57.699
to make the first ever mass-produced breakfast
pastry in the Vietnam War-era Midwest.

00:06:57.699 --> 00:07:02.870
Unfrosted has an Olympic-level cast signed
on already, including Melissa McCarthy, Amy

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.630
Schumer, and Bobby Moynihan, to name just
a few.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.710
"It's like 15 stand-up comics are in this."

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:13.110
What will come of a film brimming with some
of the 21st century's greatest comedians?

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:18.130
"You know, in my world, the wronger something
feels, the righter it is."

00:07:18.681 --> 00:07:23.010
In what will be his second release through
Netflix within a year, Jonah Hill has teamed

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:26.599
up with black-ish creator Kenya Barris to
make You People.

00:07:26.599 --> 00:07:28.960
Hill and Barris co-wrote the script together.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.450
The film examines the intersection of culture
disparities with modern love plus a sprinkling

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:38.000
of generational issues added to the mix, as
Hill and Lauren London play an interracial

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.569
couple meeting each others' families for the
first time.

00:07:40.569 --> 00:07:45.091
"So do you hang out in the hood all the time
or do you just come up here for our food and women?"

00:07:45.091 --> 00:07:50.620
As Hill and London's in-laws-to-be are Eddie
Murphy, Nia Long, Julia Louis-Dreyfus, and

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.830
David Duchovny.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:55.940
Considering Barris's success with black-ish
and Hill's ability to perfectly blend comedy

00:07:55.940 --> 00:08:01.310
and drama, You People is shaping up to be
one of the most intriguing releases of 2023.

00:08:01.712 --> 00:08:07.300
Netflix's catalog in 2023 won't be short of
action films, though Havoc might end up being

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.810
one of the streamer's best of the year.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:14.520
Directed by Gareth Evans, who last helmed
Apostle in 2018, Havoc will mark the first

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.620
non-Venom performance by Tom Hardy since Capone
in 2020.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:23.240
Havoc focuses on the aftermath of a bad drug
deal, when Hardy's detective character, Walker,

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.459
must survive within the dark underbelly of
crime in his city.

00:08:26.459 --> 00:08:30.819
Walker is tasked with saving the kidnapped
son of a high-ranking politician while watching

00:08:30.819 --> 00:08:34.550
his home unravel from the vices of greed and
corruption.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.340
As with many of Netflix's upcoming releases,
Havoc has a promising cast, highlighted by

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:43.880
Forest Whitaker, Timothy Olyphant, Justin
Cornwell, and Jessie Mei Li.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:49.200
Evans is a relatively unproven director, but
this film could completely change all that.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.570
Hardy is an exemplary leading man, so Havoc
shouldn't have any trouble finding its audience,

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:58.440
especially viewers who are fans of Netflix's
blockbuster action flick, Extraction.

00:08:59.519 --> 00:09:03.760
Director Rawson Marshall Thurber has been
tapped to helm Netflix's new dystopian thriller

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:04.779
The Division.

00:09:04.779 --> 00:09:09.430
It's his first credit since Red Notice in
2021, although he's perhaps best known for

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:14.180
directing the comedies Dodgeball: A True Underdog
Story and We're the Millers.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:19.320
The Division details how a futuristic, fast-spreading
virus is being contracted through people handling

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.320
paper money.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.900
The events reach an apex on Black Friday,
the biggest shopping day of the year, in New York City.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:31.459
What unfolds is the dissolution of society
amid a great viral catastrophe, in which the

00:09:31.459 --> 00:09:36.440
fate of the country rests in the hands of
civilians who must fight against bio-terrorists

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.930
while the government races to find a cure.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.769
As of right now, the only cast members confirmed
are Jessica Chastain and Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:09:43.769 --> 00:09:47.940
Chastain and Gyllenhaal are two of the most
reliable leading actors working in Hollywood

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:52.130
right now, so The Division should be a thrilling
story to watch.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:58.170
Step Up: All In and Pitch Perfect 3 director
Trish Sie's next film is the romantic comedy

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:01.120
Players, due to hit Netflix in late 2023.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.960
Netflix hasn't let too many cats out of the
bag about Players.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.490
All we know is that it is a rom-com with a
sports fan slant.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:11.920
A sportswriter, Mack, after years of flings
and hook-ups, meets a woman who inspires him

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.140
to settle down and go all in on a relationship.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:19.710
Tom Ellis and Jane the Virgin star Gina Rodriguez
are slated to play the movie's leads, while

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:23.960
Damon Wayans Jr., Brock O'Hurn, and Joel Courtney
will take on supporting roles.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:28.390
The last time we saw Ellis was in his leading
role on Lucifer, while Rodriguez was in the

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.760
Amazon Prime hit rom-com I Want You Back in
2022.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.320
The chemistry between Ellis and Rodriguez
will be one to look out for, as they are known

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.670
for working within different genres.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:43.705
Netflix is hit or miss with rom-coms these
days, but Players has a lot of potential.

00:10:43.705 --> 00:10:48.459
High in the Clouds is easily Netflix's most
unique impending release.

00:10:48.459 --> 00:10:53.209
An animated feature based on a children's
novel co-written by Philip Ardagh, Geoff Dunbar,

00:10:53.209 --> 00:10:58.080
and Paul McCartney in 2005, Netflix will release
it in collaboration with Gaumont sometime

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.080
this year.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:03.220
The book's illustrator, Geoff Dunbar, worked
with McCartney on the 1984 animated movie

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.750
Rupert and the Frog Song.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:09.389
High in the Clouds focuses on Woodland, an
animal home about to be demolished by humans.

00:11:09.389 --> 00:11:14.080
Wirral, a squirrel, is left orphaned by the
destruction and goes on an adventure to find

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.620
a new place to live.

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:19.380
His destination is Animalia, a sanctuary for
animals.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:24.490
Surprisingly adult, the book tackles themes
of war, loss, and companionship, and the movie

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.510
adaptation should do the same.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:31.519
The adaptation has been in development off-and-on
since 2013, with a number of filmmakers in

00:11:31.519 --> 00:11:32.700
the mix to direct.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:36.920
Officially, Head over Heels creator Timothy
Reckart will helm the film, with a script

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.610
written by Jon Croker.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:43.440
McCartney will compose songs and an original
score while also executive producing.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.649
Beatles fans and animation buffs alike are
sure to adore this film, another addition

00:11:48.649 --> 00:11:53.450
to the still-growing legacy of McCartney,
one of the world's greatest rock stars.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:58.680
In another comic book adaptation for Netflix,
Jim Mickle, co-creator of the streaming titan's

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:03.720
show Sweet Tooth, will direct his own rendition
of Donny Cates' God Country.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.889
Legendary Pictures is attached to the film,
which marks another collaboration with Netflix,

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:13.959
after the hit films Enola Holmes and Enola
Holmes 2 released in 2020 and 2022, respectively.

00:12:13.959 --> 00:12:16.839
"I am a detective.

00:12:16.839 --> 00:12:18.000
I'm a decipherer.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.590
And I'm a finder of lost souls."

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:24.050
God Country follows Emmett Quinlan, a widower
battling dementia.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:28.460
Emmett struggles with confusion, which often
leads to violent outbursts that get him in

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.899
trouble with local police and estrange him
from his family.

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:36.560
After a tornado destroys his home in West
Texas, Emmett is thought to be lost, and possibly

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.589
dead, in the debris.

00:12:37.589 --> 00:12:42.510
Instead, the disaster renders him cured and
an enchanted sword he found in the eye of

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:45.420
the storm gives him superhuman strength.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:50.190
Far from the worlds of DC and Marvel, God
Country aims to be a refreshing entry in the

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.201
superhero genre.

00:12:51.201 --> 00:12:52.420
“No capes!”

00:12:52.779 --> 00:12:57.210
No cast list or plot for the film have yet
been released, but Netflix aims to deliver

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.216
it to audiences by the end of 2023.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.300
Based on the BBC psychological thriller of
the same name, Netflix will be releasing a

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.720
film adaptation of Luther in March.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:12.410
Written by series creator Neil Cross and directed
by Jamie Payne, Luther will, as star Idris

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:16.760
Elba noted in a conversation with Empire,
"peel the onion back" on the character of

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:20.899
Luther and broaden the scope beyond just the
"gritty streets of London."

00:13:20.899 --> 00:13:26.680
"If you take me down, I'll take you down even
faster and even harder."

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:31.399
Luther enters an elite company of television
shows turned into movies, joining Charlie's

00:13:31.399 --> 00:13:35.519
Angels, The X-Files, and Star Trek, among
countless others.

00:13:35.519 --> 00:13:39.779
Elba will reprise the title role of Luther,
a police detective who has to balance the

00:13:39.779 --> 00:13:43.750
horrors of his job with the genius of his
procedural methods.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.990
Andy Serkis and Cynthia Erivo are set for
supporting roles.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:51.270
Over the course of five seasons, Luther was
well-received by audiences and critics alike.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:56.490
A BBC fan-favorite, Luther should make for
a solid film adaptation, especially with the

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:59.259
show's creator in charge of shaping the plot.

00:13:59.601 --> 00:14:05.550
Directed by George C. Wolfe, the sharp eye
behind 2020's Ma Rainey's Black Bottom, Rustin

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:10.620
is a dramatized biopic focused on the life
of gay civil rights activist Bayard Rustin.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.080
Screenwriter Dustin Lance Black, who won the
2009 Oscar for best original screenplay for

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:19.170
his Milk script, is on board to write, and
Barack and Michelle Obama's company Higher

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.709
Ground will oversee production.

00:14:21.709 --> 00:14:27.470
Rustin is set to place a big emphasis on Rustin's
organization of the 1963 March on Washington.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:31.269
Colman Domingo, who previously worked with
Wolfe in Ma Rainey's Black Bottom, is set

00:14:31.269 --> 00:14:32.339
to play Rustin.

00:14:32.339 --> 00:14:37.699
How Rustin will stack up against the seemingly
never-ending list of biopics remains to be

00:14:37.699 --> 00:14:41.839
seen, but after his success with Ma Rainey,
Wolfe appears to be the perfect man to tell

00:14:41.839 --> 00:14:43.930
the late activist's story.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:49.920
Produced by Todd Phillips, Martin Scorsese,
and Steven Spielberg, Hollywood star Bradley

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:55.269
Cooper will direct Maestro, a biopic about
composer and humanitarian Leonard Bernstein.

00:14:55.269 --> 00:15:00.720
Cooper co-wrote the movie with Josh Singer,
who won an Oscar for best original screenplay

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.079
in 2015 for his Spotlight script.

00:15:02.079 --> 00:15:05.149
"Leave something for the rest of us, Bradley
Cooper."

00:15:05.149 --> 00:15:09.370
In addition to directing, Cooper will play
Bernstein, with the film set to focus on the

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:13.740
composer's life, especially his marriage to
Felicia Montealegre, an actress who later

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:16.610
became an anti-war advocate during the Vietnam
War.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.680
Carey Mulligan will take on the role of Montealegre.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:25.080
A terrific supporting cast is already in place,
with Jeremy Strong, Matt Bomer, Maya Hawke,

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.300
and Sarah Silverman set to appear.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:31.279
Cooper's choice to use a prosthetic nose in
his portrayal of Bernstein has been met with

00:15:31.279 --> 00:15:33.560
a great deal of criticism.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:37.569
Canadian Jewish News reporter James Hirsh
proclaimed that Cooper should not be playing

00:15:37.569 --> 00:15:42.579
Bernstein at all if he is unable to do so
without the fake nose, a practical effect

00:15:42.579 --> 00:15:45.890
that plays negatively into cultural caricatures
of Jewish people.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:50.519
Maestro will certainly generate buzz come
awards season, but not without its controversies

00:15:50.519 --> 00:15:52.579
being held up to the light first.

00:15:53.579 --> 00:15:57.800
After helming the BBC film Marvellous, Julian
Farino is returning to the director's chair

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.889
for Our Man from Jersey.

00:15:59.889 --> 00:16:04.170
Mark Wahlberg is set to star, coming off his
performance in Father Stu in 2022.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:10.052
The last time we saw Wahlberg's co-star Halle
Berry was in the 2022 box office disaster Moonfall.

00:16:10.052 --> 00:16:11.620
"You are the unidentified source?"

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:12.970
"Oh, yes."

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:17.940
Our Man from Jersey tells the story of a blue-collar
man becoming a hero overnight.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:21.820
Wahlberg's character, Mike, is a construction
worker, at least until his high school girlfriend

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:25.790
Roxanne, played by Berry, convinces him to
become a spy.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:29.880
Mike is a nice guy who doesn't have any interest
in turning to the world of espionage, but

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.749
it's not long before a do-or-die mission leaves
him with no choice.

00:16:33.749 --> 00:16:39.970
J.K. Simmons, Jackie Earle Haley, Jessica De Gouw,
Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje, and Alice Lee round

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:44.380
out the cast, but few other details have been
released by Netflix so far.

00:16:44.722 --> 00:16:49.060
Not much is known about Reptile yet, other
than the fact that Grant Singer is slated

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:53.620
to direct and the cast is full of names audiences
likely wouldn't expect to see come together

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.640
in the same movie.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:59.000
Reptile marks Singer's feature film debut,
though he's spent the last nine years directing

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:03.540
music videos for Sam Smith, The Weeknd, Ariana
Grande, and Troye Sivan.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:08.220
Reptile revolves around a man named Nichols,
played by Benicio Del Toro, who is a New England

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:12.630
detective working a mysterious case that quickly
bleeds into his own personal life.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:16.991
The lines for Nichols are blurred, as he often
can't tell what's real and what's not, which

00:17:16.991 --> 00:17:19.150
leads him down a dark path.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:24.439
The cast is brimming with big names, including
Frances Fisher, Alicia Silverstone, Justin

00:17:24.439 --> 00:17:27.929
Timberlake, Eric Bogosian, Sky Ferreira, and
Michael Pitt.

00:17:27.929 --> 00:17:32.150
Reptile will mark a reunion between Silverstone
and Del Toro, who played each other's love

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.098
interest in Excess Baggage in 1997.

00:17:35.679 --> 00:17:40.270
The Spy Kids franchise is one of the most
successful live-action kids movie series of

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:46.169
all-time, grossing over $550 million worldwide
over the course of four films.

00:17:46.169 --> 00:17:51.030
Spy Kids has remained dormant for 12 years,
ever since creator Robert Rodriguez aimed

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:56.321
to shift the story's focus away from Carmen
and Juni Cortez, the stars of the first three films.

00:17:56.321 --> 00:18:00.901
"Thumb Thumbs and fooglies coming up the south
hall."

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:05.660
Spy Kids: Armageddon is meant to be a total
reboot of the series, and Rodriguez has written

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.750
the script and will be serving as director.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:12.510
The film will focus on how children are unintentionally
helping a game developer take over the world

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:16.919
through a destructive computer virus, and
must then take matters into their own hands

00:18:16.919 --> 00:18:18.750
in order to save their families.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:24.059
The cast is lead by Gina Rodriguez and Zachary
Levi, while Everly Carganilla, Connor Esterson,

00:18:24.059 --> 00:18:25.910
Billy Magnussen, and D.J.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.669
Cotrona round out the ensemble.

00:18:27.669 --> 00:18:34.059
Don't go into Spy Kids: Armageddon expecting
it to be the Citizen Kane of kids espionage movies.

00:18:34.059 --> 00:18:37.470
It probably won't dazzle critics, but it'll
be an action-packed adventure for families

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.145
on movie night.

00:18:39.145 --> 00:18:44.639
Society of the Snow is set to be one of the
most dynamic films of 2023.

00:18:44.639 --> 00:18:49.550
The only Spanish language entry on the list,
Society of the Snow is an adaptation of Pablo

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:55.370
Vierci's book The Snow Society: The Definitive
Account of the World's Greatest Survival Story,

00:18:55.370 --> 00:19:01.330
which details the experiences of the 16 survivors
from the Andes flight disaster in 1972.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:06.169
Vierci's book is particularly emotional, as
the author knew many of the survivors as a

00:19:06.169 --> 00:19:08.821
child and felt a particular connection to
them.

00:19:08.821 --> 00:19:13.010
J.A. Bayona will translate Vierci's story and documentation
onto the screen.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:18.160
The story of the Andes flight disaster is
legendary for how unfathomable the chances

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:23.990
were that anyone could withstand the mountain
range's treacherous conditions for 72 days,

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:28.650
as well as the fact that the survivors were
forced to resort to cannibalism or starve.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:33.360
"As our friends were dying, they made us realize
that we had an opportunity that they didn't.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.929
That we had a responsibility to live for them."

00:19:36.929 --> 00:19:42.270
The cast comprises mostly newcomers who don't
have any credits to their name, but interestingly,

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:46.940
Carlos Páez, one of the real-life survivors
of the flight and the youngest passenger on

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:49.690
the plane, will play his own father in the
film.

00:19:50.651 --> 00:19:55.640
Directed by MCU alums Anthony and Joe Russo,
The Electric State is an adaptation of Simon

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:57.170
Stålenhag graphic novel.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:01.030
Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely, the
brains behind the Chronicles of Narnia and

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:05.900
Captain America franchises, penned the script,
while horror filmmakers Andy and Barbara Muschietti

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.290
are slated to produce.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:11.559
Not many details about the film have been
announced, beyond the prolific ensemble cast,

00:20:11.559 --> 00:20:15.450
but the premise is said to focus on Michelle,
a young girl who looks for her missing and

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:20.040
estranged brother, who has sent her a robot
from some great, unknown place.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:23.780
The Electric State will be half-live-action
and half-animated.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.890
Frequent Netflix collaborator Millie Bobby
Brown is set to play the lead role of Michelle,

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:34.450
while Chris Pratt, Stanley Tucci, Jason Alexander,
Brian Cox, Giancarlo Esposito, and Anthony

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:37.080
Mackie are among the names rounding out the
cast.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:41.510
Be on the lookout for Ke Huy Quan, who is
fresh off his brilliant return to acting in

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:45.730
Everything Everywhere All at Once, which has
made him the best supporting actor favorite

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:47.789
at the 2023 Academy Awards.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:52.880
After ceasing production on his hit series
Mindhunter to create the blockbuster biopic

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:57.940
Mank in 2020, David Fincher has returned to
Netflix to direct The Killer, an adaptation

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:01.309
of Alexis Nolent's graphic novel series of
the same name.

00:21:01.309 --> 00:21:06.180
Fincher has been attached to Nolent's book
since as early as 2007, the project bouncing

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:10.140
from various production companies before landing
at Netflix's feet.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:15.090
Only Michael Fassbender and Tilda Swinton
have been announced as principal cast members.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:20.360
Audiences last saw Fassbender in 2019, when
he played Magneto in X-Men: Dark Phoenix.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:25.390
Swinton had a busy 2022, as she performed
in Three Thousand Years of Longing and The

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:30.799
Eternal Daughter, as well as voicing the role
of the Wood Sprite in Guillermo del Toro's Pinocchio.

00:21:30.799 --> 00:21:39.190
"To save you, he became a real boy, and real
boys don't come back."

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:45.279
Nolent's series tells the story of a nameless
assassin who makes calculated decisions quietly.

00:21:45.279 --> 00:21:49.620
Later revealed to be named Christian, he doesn't
have many goals, except for making enough

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.650
money to retire and leave the public eye completely.

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:56.919
Nolent's work is meant to test the limits
in which audiences can feel empathy for a

00:21:56.919 --> 00:21:58.200
bad person.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:02.480
If any director is capable of making that
premise work on the big screen, it's Fincher,

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:07.380
who found great success with dark, brutal
dramas, including Fight Club, Zodiac, and

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:08.380
Gone Girl.

00:22:08.602 --> 00:22:14.390
Audiences haven't seen Anthony Stacchi in
the director's chair since 2014, when he co-directed

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.200
The Boxtrolls with Graham Annable.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:17.520
"First things first.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.094
Off with the box."

00:22:20.094 --> 00:22:22.992
"Ahhhh!"

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:28.360
Known mostly for his work behind the camera,
Stacchi has built a long, storied career as

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:30.830
a storyboard artist and visual effects creator.

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:35.260
He got his start on Back to the Future in
1985, and has since worked on projects as

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:39.450
varied as Hook, James and the Giant Peach,
Antz, and Ghost.

00:22:39.450 --> 00:22:44.000
The Monkey King focuses on the titular Monkey
King, who must travel near and far to get

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.770
his staff back from the wretched Dragon King.

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:50.909
Screenwriter Steven Benchich, who wrote Brother
Bear, Chicken Little, and Open Season, penned

00:22:50.909 --> 00:22:55.580
the script, his first since Cats &amp; Dogs: The
Revenge of Kitty Galore in 2010.

00:22:55.580 --> 00:23:00.200
The Monkey King marks Benchich and Stacchi's
first collaboration since 2006.

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:07.070
A great cast is already in place, featuring
BD Wong, Jimmy O. Yang, and Bowen Yang, and

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:08.070
Stephanie Hsu.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:12.770
The Monkey King will mark the first performance
for Hsu after Everything Everywhere All at

00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:16.650
Once, which is putting her in the conversation
for best supporting actress at the Academy

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:18.470
Awards, as per Variety.

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:23.799
Matt Charman is back for his first feature
film since 2015, when he co-wrote the script

00:23:23.799 --> 00:23:26.960
for Steven Spielberg's Bridge of Spies with
the Coen Brothers.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:30.850
Charman secured an Oscar nomination for best
original screenplay, but has been awfully

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:32.180
quiet since.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:37.150
Charman's new movie, The Mothership, follows
a single mother, Sara, played by Halle Berry,

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:40.930
and her kids, who stumble upon an extraterrestrial
on their property.

00:23:40.930 --> 00:23:45.760
Sara's husband disappeared without a trace
a year earlier, and she believes her new discovery

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:49.400
will help bring him, or the truth of his whereabouts,
home.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:54.690
This marks Berry's second collaboration with
Netflix in 2023, along with Our Man from Jersey,

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:56.820
in which she stars alongside Mark Wahlberg.

00:23:56.820 --> 00:24:01.511
Molly Parker, Omari Hardwick, and Sydney Lemmon
are among the names that will round out the cast.

00:24:01.511 --> 00:24:06.890
Parker is set to have a strong 2023, as she
will also play Mary Darling in Disney's Peter

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:08.080
Pan &amp; Wendy.

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:12.529
Hardwick was last seen in the TV series Pieces
of Her, while Lemmon appeared in Tàr, alongside

00:24:12.529 --> 00:24:13.529
Cate Blanchett.

00:24:13.529 --> 00:24:19.610
A release date hasn't been set yet, but expect
The Mothership to arrive sometime in late 2023.

